# Nova-quality web shipping

When building or redesigning a **marketing site, landing page, brand site, or outreach demo** (not dashboard/app chrome inside Next.js):

1. Read and follow **`ship-marketing-site`** (`~/.cursor/skills/ship-marketing-site/SKILL.md`) — parity with Village agent Nova (`~/.openclaw/workspace/village/server/charters/nova.md`).
2. **Before any visual design**, run UI/UX Pro Max:
   ```bash
   python3 ~/.cursor/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/scripts/search.py "<product niche keywords>" --design-system
   ```
3. **Stack:** Vite+React+TS for app-y sites; static `index.html` + Tailwind CDN for simple/outreach demos.
4. **Motion:** Framer Motion, easing `[0.22, 1, 0.36, 1]`, respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
5. **Icons:** Lucide/Heroicons SVG — not emoji in UI.
6. **Solvio hospitality demos (Nova / Village):** **Required** — iframe `https://www.solviosystems.com/book/preview?lang=es|en&mode=table|appointment&name=…&wa=…`, `#reserva` / `#book`, nav CTAs. Helpers: `src/lib/outreach-demo.ts`. Rule: **`.cursor/rules/outreach-demo-site-assets.mdc`** — photos, prices, and copy from **their live site**; no unrelated stock images.
7. Ship **complete runnable files**; verify preview/build before claiming done.

Do not skip the design-system step to "save time" — that is what makes Nova sites look professional.
